<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Teutomalius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 120s BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Teutomalius was a king of the Salyes, a Celto-Ligurian people of lower Provence, in the 120s BCE. After Roman forces destroyed the Salyan stronghold of Entremont he fled to the Allobroges. Their refusal to hand him over gave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> a reason for war against the Allobroges and their Arvernian allies, which ended in 121 BCE with Roman control of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a>.</p></div>
